    "title": "Police arrest second suspect in ATM theft investigation - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Jonathan Fleig ,\n4 hours ago\nBLAKELY, LACKAWANNA COUNTY (WBRE/WYOU) — The story of that wild video out of Peckville with a stolen box truck crashing into an ATM is coming to a close: Police say they’ve arrested the second suspect they’ve been looking for.\nThey took 20-year-old Logan Konen into custody in West Hazleton on Tuesday, less than a day after putting out his arrest warrant .\nWoman accused of helping Hanover Twp. shooting suspect escape to Philly Investigators say he was linked to the January crime after talking about it and matching what was seen in that video.\nHe originally told officers he would come talk, but never showed.\nCopyright 2026 Nexstar Media, Inc. All rights reserved. This material may not be published, broadcast, rewritten, or redistributed. For the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to 28/22 News.\n1",
    "summary": "BLAKELY, LACKAWANNA COUNTY (WBRE/WYOU) — The story of that wild video out of Peckville with a stolen box truck crashing into an ATM is coming to a close: Police say they’ve arrested the second suspect they’ve been looking for. They took 20-year-old Logan Konen into custody in West Hazleton on Tuesday, less than a day after putting out his arrest warrant . shooting suspect escape to Philly Investigators say he was linked to the January crime after talking about it and matching what was seen in that video. He originally told officers he would come talk, but never showed.",
